<div class="reading">
<h1>How it works</h1>
<p><strong>A simple process. A thoughtful handoff.</strong></p>
<p><strong>Neighbors helping neighbors. Giving equipment a second life.</strong></p>
<p>FreeDME connects people who have equipment to give or lend with neighbors who need it. Equipment is offered free of charge, and participants arrange the handoff directly with one another.</p>
<section id="connect" tabindex="-1"><h2>For people giving or lending</h2>
<ol>
<li><h3>Create your account.</h3><p>Verify your phone number to get started. You may choose a display name and show your approximate location. Your phone number is not shared with other participants.</p>
</li>
<li><h3>List your equipment.</h3><p>Describe your item honestly and in as much detail as possible, including its condition and any known damage or missing parts. Add <strong>1–5 clear photographs</strong> and indicate whether you are giving it away or lending it for a specified period. You may list multiple items. A FreeDME moderator reviews each listing before it is published.</p>
</li>
<li><h3>Review requests.</h3><p>FreeDME notifies you when someone requests your item. You will see the requester’s reviewed first and last name and approximate location. You may approve the request, decline it, or indicate that the item is no longer available. You respond to <strong>one request per item at a time</strong>.</p>
</li>
<li><h3>Reserve the item and arrange the handoff.</h3><p>Once you approve a request and the requester accepts your offer, the item is reserved and removed from available listings. Use your private messages in <strong>My activity</strong> to agree on a time and a public, nonresidential meeting place.</p>
</li>
<li><h3>For a loan, agree on the return arrangements.</h3><p>Before handing over the equipment, agree with the borrower on the loan period and the date, time and public location for its return. Return arrangements are between you and the borrower. <strong>FreeDME</strong><strong> does not manage or guarantee returns.</strong></p>
</li></ol>
</section>
<section id="receiving" tabindex="-1"><h2>For people receiving or borrowing</h2>
<ol>
<li><h3>Browse available equipment.</h3><p>You can browse without creating an account.</p>
</li>
<li><h3>Verify your details before requesting an item.</h3><p>Sign in by verifying your phone number, then provide a utility bill showing your name, address and ZIP code, or a government-issued ID, such as a driver’s license, for an identity and address check.</p>
<p>A caregiver or community helper may request equipment for someone else using their own account and identity documents.</p>
</li>
<li><h3>Submit your request.</h3><p>Once your details have been reviewed, your request is sent to the donor along with your reviewed first and last name and approximate location. <strong>Your exact street address and phone number are not shared with other participants.</strong></p>
</li>
<li><h3>Accept an offer and arrange the handoff.</h3><p>The donor may approve or decline your request. If approved, accept the offer to reserve the item, then use <strong>My activity</strong> to agree on a time and a public, nonresidential meeting place. If your request is declined, you can browse for another item and submit a new request.</p>
</li>
<li><h3>Check the equipment before taking it.</h3><p>At the handoff, review the item’s condition and decide whether it is suitable for your needs. Decline anything that appears unsafe or unsuitable. For a loan, agree with the donor on the loan period and return arrangements before taking the equipment.</p>
</li></ol>
</section>
<section id="handoff" tabindex="-1" class="note warn"><h2>Meet safely</h2>
<p>Arrange every pickup and return at a <strong>public, </strong><strong>nonresidential</strong><strong> place, during daylight and while the venue is open</strong>. Home handoffs are not permitted.</p>
<p>Choose the meeting place together. FreeDME does not arrange transportation or supervise handoffs.</p>
</section>
<section id="role" tabindex="-1"><h2>Understand FreeDME’s role</h2>
<p><strong>FreeDME</strong><strong> simply connects people.</strong></p>
<p>We review listings, but we do not inspect equipment or verify the accuracy of donor-provided information. Equipment condition, features and weight capacity are reported by the donor.</p>
<p>FreeDME does not certify, fit, repair, assemble or deliver equipment, or guarantee the return of loaned items.</p>
<p>Seek qualified advice if you are unsure about an item’s suitability, fit or use. Do not put yourself at risk by testing equipment that may be unsafe.</p>
</section>
<section id="protection" tabindex="-1"><h2>Help protect the community</h2>
<p>Phone verification, review of requester identity and address information, moderator screening of listings, and tools for reporting concerns help support the community. These checks do not guarantee equipment safety or another participant’s conduct.</p>
<p>Questions and replies appear privately in the participants’ <strong>My activity</strong> pages, rather than on public listings.</p>
</section>
<section id="changes" tabindex="-1"><h2>When plans change</h2>
<p>Use <strong>My activity</strong> to cancel an arrangement or report a concern.</p>
<p>A cancellation, a missed return date or a lack of response does <strong>not</strong> automatically make a reserved item available again. The donor must confirm that the equipment is in their possession and available. Any restriction placed on the listing because of a safety concern must also be resolved before it can be listed again.</p>
</section>
<section id="response-times" tabindex="-1"><h2>Time to respond</h2>
<p><strong>For donors:</strong> If a request is awaiting your response, FreeDME sends a reminder after <strong>24 hours</strong>. If you have not responded within <strong>48 hours</strong>, the request closes.</p>
<p><strong>For requesters:</strong> Once the donor approves your request, you have <strong>24 hours</strong> to accept the offer before it expires.</p>
</section>
</div>
